WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.350
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B two.

2
00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:09.257
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.557 --> 00:00:16.296
Unit twenty-one: -ed and -ing Adjectives. Today you will describe feelings and causes with participle adjectives.

4
00:00:16.596 --> 00:00:19.295
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.233 --> 00:00:23.582
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.417 --> 00:00:25.046
Bored.

7
00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:27.515
Bored means feeling boredom.

8
00:00:28.117 --> 00:00:29.106
I am bored.

9
00:00:29.717 --> 00:00:32.137
Your turn. Say: Bored.

10
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:35.839
Bored.

11
00:00:36.583 --> 00:00:37.317
Boring.

12
00:00:38.317 --> 00:00:40.130
Boring means causing boredom.

13
00:00:40.717 --> 00:00:41.938
The talk is boring.

14
00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:44.750
Your turn. Say: Boring.

15
00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:48.508
Boring.

16
00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:50.239
Interested.

17
00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:53.284
Interested means wanting to know more.

18
00:00:53.883 --> 00:00:55.337
I'm interested in art.

19
00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:58.730
Your turn. Say: Interested.

20
00:01:01.567 --> 00:01:02.661
Interested.

21
00:01:03.417 --> 00:01:04.395
Interesting.

22
00:01:05.383 --> 00:01:07.534
Interesting means holding your attention.

23
00:01:08.150 --> 00:01:09.418
An interesting book.

24
00:01:10.017 --> 00:01:12.750
Your turn. Say: Interesting.

25
00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:16.636
Interesting.

26
00:01:17.383 --> 00:01:18.199
Tired.

27
00:01:19.183 --> 00:01:20.986
Tired means feeling tired.

28
00:01:21.583 --> 00:01:22.642
I am tired.

29
00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:25.635
Your turn. Say: Tired.

30
00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:29.339
Tired.

31
00:01:30.083 --> 00:01:30.864
Tiring.

32
00:01:31.850 --> 00:01:33.641
Tiring means making you tired.

33
00:01:34.250 --> 00:01:35.599
A tiring day.

34
00:01:36.183 --> 00:01:38.836
Your turn. Say: Tiring.

35
00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:42.631
Tiring.

36
00:01:43.383 --> 00:01:44.408
Excited.

37
00:01:45.417 --> 00:01:47.602
Excited means feeling excitement.

38
00:01:48.217 --> 00:01:49.566
We were excited.

39
00:01:50.150 --> 00:01:52.884
Your turn. Say: Excited.

40
00:01:55.733 --> 00:01:56.642
Excited.

41
00:01:57.383 --> 00:01:58.338
Exciting.

42
00:01:59.350 --> 00:02:01.570
Exciting means causing excitement.

43
00:02:02.183 --> 00:02:03.614
An exciting match.

44
00:02:04.217 --> 00:02:06.602
Your turn. Say: Exciting.

45
00:02:09.467 --> 00:02:10.445
Exciting.

46
00:02:11.233 --> 00:02:15.395
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:20.084
Visal, describe an experience with an -ed and an -ing adjective.

48
00:02:21.183 --> 00:02:33.103
The trip was exciting, and we were excited. The -ing adjective describes what causes the feeling. The -ed adjective describes how the person feels.

49
00:02:34.217 --> 00:02:36.019
What are common pairs?

50
00:02:37.117 --> 00:02:51.112
Bored and boring, interested and interesting, tired and tiring, surprised and surprising, confused and confusing. The -ed form is for feelings; the -ing form is for causes.

51
00:02:52.217 --> 00:02:53.903
What is a typical mistake?

52
00:02:55.017 --> 00:03:09.154
I am boring means I make other people bored. I am bored means I feel bored. At B2 you can also use them as modifiers: a fascinating lecture, an exhausted student, a deeply disappointing result.

53
00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:12.323
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:13.183 --> 00:03:16.646
Grammar focus: -ed (feeling) and -ing (cause) adjectives.

55
00:03:16.946 --> 00:03:18.179
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:18.883 --> 00:03:20.256
The trip was exciting.

57
00:03:21.150 --> 00:03:22.325
We were excited.

58
00:03:23.217 --> 00:03:24.891
It was a tiring journey.

59
00:03:25.833 --> 00:03:32.041
-ing = causes the feeling. -ed = feels it. I am bored (I feel it); I am boring (I cause it).

60
00:03:32.783 --> 00:03:36.446
Be careful! Don't say: I am boring in this class.

61
00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:40.841
Say: I am bored in this class.

62
00:03:41.141 --> 00:03:42.595
Use -ed for a feeling.

63
00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:46.122
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:46.933 --> 00:03:48.201
Cause and Feeling.

65
00:03:48.501 --> 00:03:50.501
The trip to the mountains was exciting.

66
00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:53.581
We were excited all the way there.

67
00:03:54.567 --> 00:03:57.286
The journey was tiring, and everyone was tired.

68
00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:01.286
The guide told interesting stories, so we were interested.

69
00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:04.567
A boring speaker would have made us bored.

70
00:04:05.667 --> 00:04:09.819
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:10.683 --> 00:04:12.033
The lecture was blank.

72
00:04:12.333 --> 00:04:16.427
A, fascinated. B, fascinating. C, fascinate.

73
00:04:19.967 --> 00:04:22.036
The answer is B: fascinating.

74
00:04:23.183 --> 00:04:24.695
I was blank by the result.

75
00:04:24.995 --> 00:04:29.125
A, surprised. B, surprising. C, surprise.

76
00:04:32.667 --> 00:04:34.562
The answer is A: surprised.

77
00:04:35.717 --> 00:04:37.333
Which means 'I feel bored'?

78
00:04:37.633 --> 00:04:42.018
A, I am boring.. B, I am bored.. C, I am bore..

79
00:04:45.567 --> 00:04:47.810
The answer is B: I am bored..

80
00:04:48.950 --> 00:04:51.727
A film that makes people excited is blank.

81
00:04:52.027 --> 00:04:56.018
A, exciting. B, excited. C, excite.

82
00:04:59.567 --> 00:05:01.508
The answer is A: exciting.

83
00:05:02.650 --> 00:05:05.903
According to the reading, who told interesting stories?

84
00:05:06.203 --> 00:05:10.043
A, the guide. B, the driver. C, the teacher.

85
00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:15.681
The answer is A: the guide.

86
00:05:16.867 --> 00:05:19.891
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:24.410
Describe an experience using both an -ed and an -ing adjective.

88
00:05:33.217 --> 00:05:34.949
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:35.249 --> 00:05:47.770
The museum visit was fascinating, and I was amazed by the old pictures. The guide was friendly, but the long walk was tiring, so we were exhausted by the end.

90
00:05:48.070 --> 00:05:49.744
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:50.650 --> 00:05:55.520
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and -ed (feeling) and -ing (cause) adjectives.

92
00:05:55.820 --> 00:06:00.899
Today's value is appreciation of beauty. Learn to notice and value the beauty around you.

93
00:06:01.199 --> 00:06:04.025
See you in Unit twenty-two. Goodbye!

94
00:06:04.325 --> 00:06:07.744
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

